{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4HrYuU29AARn7B7RWQ95b","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md b/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\nindex 2b866ef3..5f261301 100644\n--- a/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\n+++ b/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n ## Status\n \n-Proposed — 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35. The transport, the identity and the slicing of B35 are decided by the amendment at the end (2026-11-09). No IPC, cache API/schema, daemon lifecycle,\n+Proposed — 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35; the optional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices and the delivered state, with where it departs from the decisions above, is the last amendment (2026-11-10). The transport, the identity and the slicing of B35 are decided by the amendment at the end (2026-11-09). No IPC, cache API/schema, daemon lifecycle,\n platform default or policy is implemented/adopted by this proposal. Reconcile and\n resolve the structural contract before functional start. Preserve accepted ADRs\n for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the\n@@ -267,3 +267,43 @@ Decided 2026-11-09 with the maintainer, before the functional start of B35:\n   protected from heavy checks, measured thresholds). Budgets and thresholds are\n   fixed from a measured synthetic corpus with a declared environment, never from a\n   historical sample.\n+\n+## Amendment: what the optional worktree runtime delivered, and where it departs (B35, 2026-11-10)\n+\n+The three slices are done and each was reviewed independently: `pose-optional-worktree-runtime`\n+(identity, protected endpoint, handshake, lifecycle, standalone fallback),\n+`pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache` (hosted read checks, typed results, resident memo) and\n+`pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement` (admission lanes and the measurement), with two engine\n+specs that the measurements called for (`pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once`,\n+`pose-governance-audit-skips-pure-git-reads`). The statement above that \"the runtime of slice 1\n+hosts no domain operation\" was true of slice 1 only. What stands now, and what differs from the\n+decisions of this ADR:\n+\n+- **Hosted operations.** The runtime hosts five read checks (`review-check`, `closeout-check`,\n+  `artifact-check`, `surface-check`, `roadmap-check`) through `pose runtime run`, as the user that\n+  started it, in its worktree; a hosted request carries the caller's identity and is refused,\n+  before any handler runs, when it does not match the runtime's engine, build, protocol, schema\n+  or worktree; the caller's environment digest must equal the runtime's. They are not writes, but\n+  they may refresh derived files as they do standalone (published atomically); a command that may\n+  have run (deadline, lost reply) is never repeated elsewhere unasked, which is how the decision\n+  \"an ambiguous committed write requires a receipt before a retry\" is met for these commands.\n+  Hosted commands go through the domain's own entry (`mainCommand`), not a new typed interface:\n+  the typed-domain extraction of the first bullet of the decision stays with B31.\n+- **Caches.** The B33 views are not what the runtime reuses (the measurements showed they do not\n+  address the cost). It keeps, between commands, the output of the Git reads that are pure\n+  functions of object ids or of the commit HEAD named when they ran, keyed by the commit, the\n+  content of the shallow file and of the repository config, with a byte budget and\n+  least-recently-used eviction; no watcher exists, so \"watch events are hints\" is met by not\n+  using them: freshness comes from the key, and nothing about mtime or a clean tree is taken as\n+  proof. The scoped Git batch reader is untouched.\n+- **Budgets and QoS.** Admission is by two lanes (`short`, `heavy`) with slots and bounded queues\n+  and a bound on the memo; the global concurrency bound is the sum of the slots. **Not delivered:**\n+  CPU quota or affinity awareness, and per-command memory or I/O limits; the runtime bounds what\n+  it admits and keeps, not what each command consumes. The measurement records latency, the\n+  runtime's resident set and CPU time per scenario, including two simultaneous heavy checks, on one\n+  environment; it is not a general benchmark.\n+- **Platforms.** Unix domain socket on Linux and macOS (credentials of the peer from the\n+  operating system); Windows runs every command standalone and `pose runtime status` says so.\n+  The named pipe is a follow-up.\n+- **Status.** The decision stands as amended for the delivered scope; what is not delivered above\n+  is not adopted and needs its own spec before it is claimed.\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md\nindex 2f804748..d55308e0 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md\n@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ Fatia 3 da B35 (emenda do ADR de 2026-11-09). Depois da fatia 2 o runtime rodava\n - [x] Flags de admissão em `start`/`serve` e repasse ao `serve` destacado\n - [x] Harness de medição com amostras, cenários e limiares fixados\n - [x] Rodar a medição e registrar o relatório\n-- [ ] Revisão independente e fechamento\n+- [x] Revisão independente e fechamento\n \n ## 5. Decisions\n \ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\nindex f2601438..d8d919d6 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Fatia 2 da B35 (emenda do ADR de 2026-11-09), reescrita pela medição que as du\n - [x] Handler hospedado: admissão, digest de ambiente, um por vez\n - [x] `pose runtime run` com fallback standalone e sem repetir o que pode ter rodado\n - [x] Medir: o segundo `review-check` no runtime contra standalone, com a saída comparada\n-- [ ] Revisão independente e fechamento\n+- [x] Revisão independente e fechamento\n \n ## 5. Decisions\n \n@@ -134,5 +134,5 @@ O runtime hospeda `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check`, `surface-c\n \n - [open] Test the admission of a memo hit's bytes against an operation's input budget when the budget is nearly spent. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n - [open] Put the user and global Git configuration in the memo key, as the repository's own is. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n-- [open] Admissão, orçamento e proteção das consultas curtas contra checks pesados, com medições fixadas (fatia 3, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-02-08)\n+- [covered: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement] Admissão, orçamento e proteção das consultas curtas contra checks pesados, com medições fixadas (fatia 3, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-02-08)\n - [open] Rotear os checks para o runtime quando ele existe, sem `run` explícito, e renderizar para terminal. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\nindex e0ae77b6..a892771e 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\n@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ const (\n \tthresholdShortFloorMS    = 250  // ... or 250 ms, whichever is more\n \tthresholdRSSMiB          = 1536 // resident set of the runtime after the warm runs\n \tthresholdFallbackExtraMS = 500  // trying a runtime that is not there costs at most this\n+\tthresholdTwoHeavyOverOne = 2.5  // T7: two simultaneous heavy checks on the one heavy slot: wall <= 2.5 x one warm run\n )\n \n type measureReport struct {\n@@ -45,6 +46,32 @@ type measureReport struct {\n \tVerdicts    map[string]string  `json:\"verdicts\"`\n }\n \n+// runtimeProc reads the runtime process's cumulative CPU time (user + system, ms) and its\n+// resident set (MiB) from /proc; ok is false where there is none.\n+func runtimeProc(pid int) (cpuMS int64, rssMiB float64, ok bool) {\n+\tstat, err := os.ReadFile(\"/proc/\" + strconv.Itoa(pid) + \"/stat\")\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn 0, 0, false\n+\t}\n+\t// The command name is in parentheses and may hold spaces: fields count from after it.\n+\ttext := string(stat)\n+\tfields := strings.Fields(text[strings.LastIndex(text, \")\")+2:])\n+\tif len(fields) < 13 {\n+\t\treturn 0, 0, false\n+\t}\n+\tutime, _ := strconv.ParseInt(fields[11], 10, 64)\n+\tstime, _ := strconv.ParseInt(fields[12], 10, 64)\n+\tstatus, _ := os.ReadFile(\"/proc/\" + strconv.Itoa(pid) + \"/status\")\n+\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(string(status), \"\\n\") {\n+\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(line, \"VmRSS:\") {\n+\t\t\tkb, _ := strconv.ParseFloat(strings.Fields(line)[1], 64)\n+\t\t\trssMiB = kb / 1024\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tconst clockTicksPerSecond = 100\n+\treturn (utime + stime) * 1000 / clockTicksPerSecond, rssMiB, true\n+}\n+\n func measureMedian(v []int64) int64 {\n \ts := append([]int64(nil), v...)\n \tsort.Slice(s, func(i, j int) bool { return s[i] < s[j] })\n@@ -163,6 +190,26 @@ func TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"start: %s\", o)\n \t}\n \tdefer run(\"runtime\", \"stop\")\n+\tpidOf := func() int {\n+\t\to, _, _ := run(\"runtime\", \"status\", \"--json\")\n+\t\tvar d struct {\n+\t\t\tPID int `json:\"pid\"`\n+\t\t}\n+\t\t_ = json.Unmarshal([]byte(strings.SplitN(o, \"\\x00\", 2)[0]), &d)\n+\t\treturn d.PID\n+\t}\n+\tpid := pidOf()\n+\t// Per scenario: the CPU time the runtime process spent and its resident set afterwards.\n+\tmark := func(scenario string, since int64) int64 {\n+\t\tcpu, rss, ok := runtimeProc(pid)\n+\t\tif ok {\n+\t\t\trep.Figures[\"cpu_ms_\"+scenario] = float64(cpu - since)\n+\t\t\trep.Figures[\"rss_mib_after_\"+scenario] = rss\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn cpu\n+\t}\n+\tcpuNow := func() int64 { cpu, _, _ := runtimeProc(pid); return cpu }\n+\tcpuBefore := cpuNow()\n \tfor i := 0; i < measureWarmSamples+1; i++ {\n \t\to, ms, via := runtimeRun(\"review-check\", spec)\n \t\tif via != \"runtime\" || o != coldOut {\n@@ -174,6 +221,7 @@ func TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t\trep.Scenarios[\"resident_warm\"] = append(rep.Scenarios[\"resident_warm\"], ms)\n \t\t}\n \t}\n+\tmark(\"resident_first_and_warm\", cpuBefore)\n \twarm := measureMedian(rep.Scenarios[\"resident_warm\"])\n \trep.Figures[\"warm_over_cold\"] = float64(warm) / float64(cold)\n \tif float64(warm) <= thresholdWarmOverCold*float64(cold) {\n@@ -191,6 +239,9 @@ func TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t}\n \t\trep.Scenarios[\"short_idle\"] = append(rep.Scenarios[\"short_idle\"], ms)\n \t}\n+\tcpuIdleShortEnd := cpuNow()\n+\t_ = cpuIdleShortEnd\n+\tcpuHeavyStart := cpuNow()\n \tvar wg sync.WaitGroup\n \twg.Add(1)\n \tgo func() { defer wg.Done(); runtimeRun(\"review-check\", spec) }()\n@@ -203,6 +254,29 @@ func TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository(t *testing.T) {\n \t\trep.Scenarios[\"short_under_heavy\"] = append(rep.Scenarios[\"short_under_heavy\"], ms)\n \t}\n \twg.Wait()\n+\tmark(\"heavy_with_short_queries\", cpuHeavyStart)\n+\t// S6: two heavy checks at once on the one heavy slot: the second waits its turn.\n+\ttwoStart := time.Now()\n+\tcpuTwo := cpuNow()\n+\tvar two [2]string\n+\tvar twoVia [2]string\n+\tvar wg2 sync.WaitGroup\n+\tfor k := 0; k < 2; k++ {\n+\t\twg2.Add(1)\n+\t\tgo func(k int) { defer wg2.Done(); two[k], _, twoVia[k] = runtimeRun(\"review-check\", spec) }(k)\n+\t}\n+\twg2.Wait()\n+\ttwoWall := time.Since(twoStart).Milliseconds()\n+\tmark(\"two_simultaneous_heavy\", cpuTwo)\n+\trep.Scenarios[\"two_heavy_wall\"] = []int64{twoWall}\n+\trep.Figures[\"two_heavy_over_one_warm\"] = float64(twoWall) / float64(warm)\n+\tif two[0] != coldOut || two[1] != coldOut || twoVia[0] != \"runtime\" || twoVia[1] != \"runtime\" {\n+\t\tfail(\"T7 two simultaneous heavy checks\", \"via %v, outputs equal to standalone %v %v\", twoVia, two[0] == coldOut, two[1] == coldOut)\n+\t} else if float64(twoWall) <= thresholdTwoHeavyOverOne*float64(warm) {\n+\t\tpass(\"T7 two simultaneous heavy checks\", \"both through the runtime with the standalone output; wall %d ms <= %.1f x %d ms\", twoWall, thresholdTwoHeavyOverOne, warm)\n+\t} else {\n+\t\tfail(\"T7 two simultaneous heavy checks\", \"wall %d ms > %.1f x %d ms\", twoWall, thresholdTwoHeavyOverOne, warm)\n+\t}\n \tidle, loaded := measureP95(rep.Scenarios[\"short_idle\"]), measureP95(rep.Scenarios[\"short_under_heavy\"])\n \tbound := int64(thresholdShortUnderHeavy * float64(idle))\n \tif bound < thresholdShortFloorMS {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\nindex 5ad317f0..fdab1685 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\n@@ -2,7 +2,8 @@ package pose\n \n import (\n \t\"container/list\"\n-\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n+\t\"encoding/hex\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n \t\"strings\"\n@@ -63,15 +64,19 @@ func residentGitKey(root, head string, args []string) (string, bool) {\n \tif err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n \t\treturn \"\", false\n \t}\n-\tshallow := \"-\"\n-\tif s, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(gitDir, \"shallow\")); err == nil {\n-\t\tshallow = fmt.Sprintf(\"%d:%d\", s.Size(), s.ModTime().UnixNano())\n+\t// The shallow file and the repository config are small: their content, not a timestamp,\n+\t// is part of the key.\n+\tdigestOf := func(name string) string {\n+\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(gitDir, name))\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn \"-\"\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tsum := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n+\t\treturn hex.EncodeToString(sum[:8])\n \t}\n+\tshallow := digestOf(\"shallow\")\n \t// The repository's own config can change what a read answers (log.follow, for one).\n-\tconfig := \"-\"\n-\tif c, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(gitDir, \"config\")); err == nil {\n-\t\tconfig = fmt.Sprintf(\"%d:%d\", c.Size(), c.ModTime().UnixNano())\n-\t}\n+\tconfig := digestOf(\"config\")\n \treturn strings.Join([]string{filepath.Clean(root), head, shallow, config, strings.Join(args, \"\\x00\")}, \"\\x01\"), true\n }\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go b/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\nindex 6d971373..e75d67e8 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\n@@ -443,6 +443,17 @@ func (s *server) handle(ctx context.Context, conn net.Conn) {\n \t\twriteReply(conn, reply)\n \tdefault:\n \t\tif s.opts.Handler != nil {\n+\t\t\t// A hosted operation is its own handshake: it carries the caller's identity, and a\n+\t\t\t// caller of another engine, build, protocol, schema or worktree is refused before the\n+\t\t\t// handler sees it, whatever the caller handshook with a moment before.\n+\t\t\tif req.Identity == nil {\n+\t\t\t\twriteReply(conn, Reply{Error: \"a hosted operation carries the caller's identity\"})\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif mism := s.opts.Identity.Mismatches(*req.Identity); len(mism) > 0 {\n+\t\t\t\twriteReply(conn, Reply{Mismatch: mism, Error: \"incompatible\", PID: os.Getpid()})\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t\t// The reply of a long operation must still be writable.\n \t\t\t_ = conn.SetDeadline(time.Now().Add(hostedDuration(req.DeadlineMS) + requestDeadline))\n \t\t\tif reply, ok := s.opts.Handler(ctx, req); ok {\n@@ -458,7 +469,7 @@ func (s *server) handle(ctx context.Context, conn net.Conn) {\n \n // drain waits, up to the deadline, for the requests in flight besides this one.\n func (s *server) drain(deadline time.Duration) Reply {\n-\tbefore := s.inflight.Load() - 1\n+\tbefore := s.inflight.Load() + s.busy() - 1\n \tend := time.Now().Add(deadline)\n \tfor s.inflight.Load()+s.busy() > 1 && time.Now().Before(end) {\n \t\ttime.Sleep(5 * time.Millisecond)\n@@ -603,12 +614,19 @@ func hostedDuration(deadlineMS int) time.Duration {\n // Run sends a hosted operation: the command line, the digest of the caller's environment and\n // the longest it may take (zero for the runtime's default).\n func (c Client) Run(ctx context.Context, args []string, env string, deadline time.Duration) (Reply, error) {\n-\treturn c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: \"run\", Args: args, Env: env, DeadlineMS: int(deadline.Milliseconds())})\n+\tid := c.Identity\n+\treply, err := c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: \"run\", Identity: &id, Args: args, Env: env, DeadlineMS: int(deadline.Milliseconds())})\n+\tif err == nil && len(reply.Mismatch) > 0 {\n+\t\t// Refused before it started: the caller falls back, as for any incompatible runtime.\n+\t\treturn reply, &IncompatibleError{Mismatch: reply.Mismatch}\n+\t}\n+\treturn reply, err\n }\n \n // Do sends an operation the runtime hosts and returns its reply.\n func (c Client) Do(ctx context.Context, op string) (Reply, error) {\n-\treturn c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: op})\n+\tid := c.Identity\n+\treturn c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: op, Identity: &id})\n }\n \n // WaitReleased returns when the endpoint of the identity can be taken: nothing answers and the\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime_test.go\nindex ab19424c..3d4dc56d 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime_test.go\n@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ import (\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n \t\"runtime\"\n \t\"strings\"\n+\t\"sync/atomic\"\n \t\"testing\"\n \t\"time\"\n )\n@@ -415,3 +416,74 @@ func TestAReplyDoesNotEscapeHTMLCharacters(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"the reply escapes HTML characters: %s\", raw)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// A hosted operation is its own handshake: a caller whose engine differs from the runtime's is\n+// refused before the handler runs, even if it handshook with an earlier runtime a moment before.\n+func TestAHostedOperationFromAnotherEngineIsRefusedBeforeTheHandlerRuns(t *testing.T) {\n+\tskipUnsupported(t)\n+\tid := identity(t, repo(t), \"7.4.1\")\n+\tdir := shortDir(t)\n+\tvar ran atomic.Int64\n+\tctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())\n+\tdefer cancel()\n+\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n+\tgo func() {\n+\t\tdone <- Serve(ctx, Options{Identity: id, Dir: dir, Handler: func(_ context.Context, req Request) (Reply, bool) {\n+\t\t\tif req.Op != \"run\" {\n+\t\t\t\treturn Reply{}, false\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tran.Add(1)\n+\t\t\treturn Reply{Outcome: OutcomeCompleted}, true\n+\t\t}})\n+\t}()\n+\tc := Client{Identity: id, Dir: dir}\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 200; i++ {\n+\t\tif _, err := c.Status(context.Background()); err == nil {\n+\t\t\tbreak\n+\t\t}\n+\t\ttime.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := c.Run(context.Background(), []string{\"review-check\"}, \"env\", 0); err != nil || ran.Load() != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a caller of the same identity: %v, ran %d\", err, ran.Load())\n+\t}\n+\tother := c\n+\tother.Identity.Engine = \"7.5.0\"\n+\t_, err := other.Run(context.Background(), []string{\"review-check\"}, \"env\", 0)\n+\tvar inc *IncompatibleError\n+\tif !errors.As(err, &inc) || ran.Load() != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a caller of another engine: %v, ran %d\", err, ran.Load())\n+\t}\n+\t// A request with no identity at all is refused too.\n+\treply, err := c.roundTrip(context.Background(), Request{Op: \"run\"})\n+\tif err != nil || reply.OK || ran.Load() != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a hosted request without an identity: %+v %v ran %d\", reply, err, ran.Load())\n+\t}\n+\tcancel()\n+\t<-done\n+}\n+\n+// A command past its deadline is counted by the stop as what it abandoned, never as a negative\n+// drain.\n+func TestAStopCountsWhatARunningCommandAbandonsAndNeverReportsANegativeDrain(t *testing.T) {\n+\tskipUnsupported(t)\n+\tid := identity(t, repo(t), \"7.4.1\")\n+\tdir := shortDir(t)\n+\tvar busy atomic.Int64\n+\tbusy.Store(1)\n+\tctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())\n+\tdefer cancel()\n+\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n+\tgo func() { done <- Serve(ctx, Options{Identity: id, Dir: dir, Busy: busy.Load}) }()\n+\tc := Client{Identity: id, Dir: dir}\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 200; i++ {\n+\t\tif _, err := c.Status(context.Background()); err == nil {\n+\t\t\tbreak\n+\t\t}\n+\t\ttime.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)\n+\t}\n+\treply, err := c.Stop(context.Background(), 100*time.Millisecond)\n+\tif err != nil || reply.Abandoned != 1 || reply.Drained != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"stop with a command still running: %+v %v\", reply, err)\n+\t}\n+\t<-done\n+}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"545c8c58-a276-4872-b4ad-2928e000cdec","timestamp":"2026-11-10T10:37:48.933Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md b/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\nindex 2b866ef3..5f261301 100644\n--- a/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\n+++ b/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n ## Status\n \n-Proposed — 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35. The transport, the identity and the slicing of B35 are decided by the amendment at the end (2026-11-09). No IPC, cache API/schema, daemon lifecycle,\n+Proposed — 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35; the optional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices and the delivered state, with where it departs from the decisions above, is the last amendment (2026-11-10). The transport, the identity and the slicing of B35 are decided by the amendment at the end (2026-11-09). No IPC, cache API/schema, daemon lifecycle,\n platform default or policy is implemented/adopted by this proposal. Reconcile and\n resolve the structural contract before functional start. Preserve accepted ADRs\n for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the\n@@ -267,3 +267,43 @@ Decided 2026-11-09 with the maintainer, before the functional start of B35:\n   protected from heavy checks, measured thresholds). Budgets and thresholds are\n   fixed from a measured synthetic corpus with a declared environment, never from a\n   historical sample.\n+\n+## Amendment: what the optional worktree runtime delivered, and where it departs (B35, 2026-11-10)\n+\n+The three slices are done and each was reviewed independently: `pose-optional-worktree-runtime`\n+(identity, protected endpoint, handshake, lifecycle, standalone fallback),\n+`pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache` (hosted read checks, typed results, resident memo) and\n+`pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement` (admission lanes and the measurement), with two engine\n+specs that the measurements called for (`pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once`,\n+`pose-governance-audit-skips-pure-git-reads`). The statement above that \"the runtime of slice 1\n+hosts no domain operation\" was true of slice 1 only. What stands now, and what differs from the\n+decisions of this ADR:\n+\n+- **Hosted operations.** The runtime hosts five read checks (`review-check`, `closeout-check`,\n+  `artifact-check`, `surface-check`, `roadmap-check`) through `pose runtime run`, as the user that\n+  started it, in its worktree; a hosted request carries the caller's identity and is refused,\n+  before any handler runs, when it does not match the runtime's engine, build, protocol, schema\n+  or worktree; the caller's environment digest must equal the runtime's. They are not writes, but\n+  they may refresh derived files as they do standalone (published atomically); a command that may\n+  have run (deadline, lost reply) is never repeated elsewhere unasked, which is how the decision\n+  \"an ambiguous committed write requires a receipt before a retry\" is met for these commands.\n+  Hosted commands go through the domain's own entry (`mainCommand`), not a new typed interface:\n+  the typed-domain extraction of the first bullet of the decision stays with B31.\n+- **Caches.** The B33 views are not what the runtime reuses (the measurements showed they do not\n+  address the cost). It keeps, between commands, the output of the Git reads that are pure\n+  functions of object ids or of the commit HEAD named when they ran, keyed by the commit, the\n+  content of the shallow file and of the repository config, with a byte budget and\n+  least-recently-used eviction; no watcher exists, so \"watch events are hints\" is met by not\n+  using them: freshness comes from the key, and nothing about mtime or a clean tree is taken as\n+  proof. The scoped Git batch reader is untouched.\n+- **Budgets and QoS.** Admission is by two lanes (`short`, `heavy`) with slots and bounded queues\n+  and a bound on the memo; the global concurrency bound is the sum of the slots. **Not delivered:**\n+  CPU quota or affinity awareness, and per-command memory or I/O limits; the runtime bounds what\n+  it admits and keeps, not what each command consumes. The measurement records latency, the\n+  runtime's resident set and CPU time per scenario, including two simultaneous heavy checks, on one\n+  environment; it is not a general benchmark.\n+- **Platforms.** Unix domain socket on Linux and macOS (credentials of the peer from the\n+  operating system); Windows runs every command standalone and `pose runtime status` says so.\n+  The named pipe is a follow-up.\n+- **Status.** The decision stands as amended for the delivered scope; what is not delivered above\n+  is not adopted and needs its own spec before it is claimed.\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md\nindex 2f804748..d55308e0 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md\n@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ Fatia 3 da B35 (emenda do ADR de 2026-11-09). Depois da fatia 2 o runtime rodava\n - [x] Flags de admissão em `start`/`serve` e repasse ao `serve` destacado\n - [x] Harness de medição com amostras, cenários e limiares fixados\n - [x] Rodar a medição e registrar o relatório\n-- [ ] Revisão independente e fechamento\n+- [x] Revisão independente e fechamento\n \n ## 5. Decisions\n \ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\nindex f2601438..d8d919d6 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Fatia 2 da B35 (emenda do ADR de 2026-11-09), reescrita pela medição que as du\n - [x] Handler hospedado: admissão, digest de ambiente, um por vez\n - [x] `pose runtime run` com fallback standalone e sem repetir o que pode ter rodado\n - [x] Medir: o segundo `review-check` no runtime contra standalone, com a saída comparada\n-- [ ] Revisão independente e fechamento\n+- [x] Revisão independente e fechamento\n \n ## 5. Decisions\n \n@@ -134,5 +134,5 @@ O runtime hospeda `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check`, `surface-c\n \n - [open] Test the admission of a memo hit's bytes against an operation's input budget when the budget is nearly spent. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n - [open] Put the user and global Git configuration in the memo key, as the repository's own is. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n-- [open] Admissão, orçamento e proteção das consultas curtas contra checks pesados, com medições fixadas (fatia 3, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-02-08)\n+- [covered: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement] Admissão, orçamento e proteção das consultas curtas contra checks pesados, com medições fixadas (fatia 3, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-02-08)\n - [open] Rotear os checks para o runtime quando ele existe, sem `run` explícito, e renderizar para terminal. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\nindex e0ae77b6..a892771e 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\n@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ const (\n \tthresholdShortFloorMS    = 250  // ... or 250 ms, whichever is more\n \tthresholdRSSMiB          = 1536 // resident set of the runtime after the warm runs\n \tthresholdFallbackExtraMS = 500  // trying a runtime that is not there costs at most this\n+\tthresholdTwoHeavyOverOne = 2.5  // T7: two simultaneous heavy checks on the one heavy slot: wall <= 2.5 x one warm run\n )\n \n type measureReport struct {\n@@ -45,6 +46,32 @@ type measureReport struct {\n \tVerdicts    map[string]string  `json:\"verdicts\"`\n }\n \n+// runtimeProc reads the runtime process's cumulative CPU time (user + system, ms) and its\n+// resident set (MiB) from /proc; ok is false where there is none.\n+func runtimeProc(pid int) (cpuMS int64, rssMiB float64, ok bool) {\n+\tstat, err := os.ReadFile(\"/proc/\" + strconv.Itoa(pid) + \"/stat\")\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn 0, 0, false\n+\t}\n+\t// The command name is in parentheses and may hold spaces: fields count from after it.\n+\ttext := string(stat)\n+\tfields := strings.Fields(text[strings.LastIndex(text, \")\")+2:])\n+\tif len(fields) < 13 {\n+\t\treturn 0, 0, false\n+\t}\n+\tutime, _ := strconv.ParseInt(fields[11], 10, 64)\n+\tstime, _ := strconv.ParseInt(fields[12], 10, 64)\n+\tstatus, _ := os.ReadFile(\"/proc/\" + strconv.Itoa(pid) + \"/status\")\n+\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(string(status), \"\\n\") {\n+\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(line, \"VmRSS:\") {\n+\t\t\tkb, _ := strconv.ParseFloat(strings.Fields(line)[1], 64)\n+\t\t\trssMiB = kb / 1024\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tconst clockTicksPerSecond = 100\n+\treturn (utime + stime) * 1000 / clockTicksPerSecond, rssMiB, true\n+}\n+\n func measureMedian(v []int64) int64 {\n \ts := append([]int64(nil), v...)\n \tsort.Slice(s, func(i, j int) bool { return s[i] < s[j] })\n@@ -163,6 +190,26 @@ func TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"start: %s\", o)\n \t}\n \tdefer run(\"runtime\", \"stop\")\n+\tpidOf := func() int {\n+\t\to, _, _ := run(\"runtime\", \"status\", \"--json\")\n+\t\tvar d struct {\n+\t\t\tPID int `json:\"pid\"`\n+\t\t}\n+\t\t_ = json.Unmarshal([]byte(strings.SplitN(o, \"\\x00\", 2)[0]), &d)\n+\t\treturn d.PID\n+\t}\n+\tpid := pidOf()\n+\t// Per scenario: the CPU time the runtime process spent and its resident set afterwards.\n+\tmark := func(scenario string, since int64) int64 {\n+\t\tcpu, rss, ok := runtimeProc(pid)\n+\t\tif ok {\n+\t\t\trep.Figures[\"cpu_ms_\"+scenario] = float64(cpu - since)\n+\t\t\trep.Figures[\"rss_mib_after_\"+scenario] = rss\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn cpu\n+\t}\n+\tcpuNow := func() int64 { cpu, _, _ := runtimeProc(pid); return cpu }\n+\tcpuBefore := cpuNow()\n \tfor i := 0; i < measureWarmSamples+1; i++ {\n \t\to, ms, via := runtimeRun(\"review-check\", spec)\n \t\tif via != \"runtime\" || o != coldOut {\n@@ -174,6 +221,7 @@ func TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t\trep.Scenarios[\"resident_warm\"] = append(rep.Scenarios[\"resident_warm\"], ms)\n \t\t}\n \t}\n+\tmark(\"resident_first_and_warm\", cpuBefore)\n \twarm := measureMedian(rep.Scenarios[\"resident_warm\"])\n \trep.Figures[\"warm_over_cold\"] = float64(warm) / float64(cold)\n \tif float64(warm) <= thresholdWarmOverCold*float64(cold) {\n@@ -191,6 +239,9 @@ func TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t}\n \t\trep.Scenarios[\"short_idle\"] = append(rep.Scenarios[\"short_idle\"], ms)\n \t}\n+\tcpuIdleShortEnd := cpuNow()\n+\t_ = cpuIdleShortEnd\n+\tcpuHeavyStart := cpuNow()\n \tvar wg sync.WaitGroup\n \twg.Add(1)\n \tgo func() { defer wg.Done(); runtimeRun(\"review-check\", spec) }()\n@@ -203,6 +254,29 @@ func TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository(t *testing.T) {\n \t\trep.Scenarios[\"short_under_heavy\"] = append(rep.Scenarios[\"short_under_heavy\"], ms)\n \t}\n \twg.Wait()\n+\tmark(\"heavy_with_short_queries\", cpuHeavyStart)\n+\t// S6: two heavy checks at once on the one heavy slot: the second waits its turn.\n+\ttwoStart := time.Now()\n+\tcpuTwo := cpuNow()\n+\tvar two [2]string\n+\tvar twoVia [2]string\n+\tvar wg2 sync.WaitGroup\n+\tfor k := 0; k < 2; k++ {\n+\t\twg2.Add(1)\n+\t\tgo func(k int) { defer wg2.Done(); two[k], _, twoVia[k] = runtimeRun(\"review-check\", spec) }(k)\n+\t}\n+\twg2.Wait()\n+\ttwoWall := time.Since(twoStart).Milliseconds()\n+\tmark(\"two_simultaneous_heavy\", cpuTwo)\n+\trep.Scenarios[\"two_heavy_wall\"] = []int64{twoWall}\n+\trep.Figures[\"two_heavy_over_one_warm\"] = float64(twoWall) / float64(warm)\n+\tif two[0] != coldOut || two[1] != coldOut || twoVia[0] != \"runtime\" || twoVia[1] != \"runtime\" {\n+\t\tfail(\"T7 two simultaneous heavy checks\", \"via %v, outputs equal to standalone %v %v\", twoVia, two[0] == coldOut, two[1] == coldOut)\n+\t} else if float64(twoWall) <= thresholdTwoHeavyOverOne*float64(warm) {\n+\t\tpass(\"T7 two simultaneous heavy checks\", \"both through the runtime with the standalone output; wall %d ms <= %.1f x %d ms\", twoWall, thresholdTwoHeavyOverOne, warm)\n+\t} else {\n+\t\tfail(\"T7 two simultaneous heavy checks\", \"wall %d ms > %.1f x %d ms\", twoWall, thresholdTwoHeavyOverOne, warm)\n+\t}\n \tidle, loaded := measureP95(rep.Scenarios[\"short_idle\"]), measureP95(rep.Scenarios[\"short_under_heavy\"])\n \tbound := int64(thresholdShortUnderHeavy * float64(idle))\n \tif bound < thresholdShortFloorMS {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\nindex 5ad317f0..fdab1685 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\n@@ -2,7 +2,8 @@ package pose\n \n import (\n \t\"container/list\"\n-\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n+\t\"encoding/hex\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n \t\"strings\"\n@@ -63,15 +64,19 @@ func residentGitKey(root, head string, args []string) (string, bool) {\n \tif err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n \t\treturn \"\", false\n \t}\n-\tshallow := \"-\"\n-\tif s, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(gitDir, \"shallow\")); err == nil {\n-\t\tshallow = fmt.Sprintf(\"%d:%d\", s.Size(), s.ModTime().UnixNano())\n+\t// The shallow file and the repository config are small: their content, not a timestamp,\n+\t// is part of the key.\n+\tdigestOf := func(name string) string {\n+\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(gitDir, name))\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn \"-\"\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tsum := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n+\t\treturn hex.EncodeToString(sum[:8])\n \t}\n+\tshallow := digestOf(\"shallow\")\n \t// The repository's own config can change what a read answers (log.follow, for one).\n-\tconfig := \"-\"\n-\tif c, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(gitDir, \"config\")); err == nil {\n-\t\tconfig = fmt.Sprintf(\"%d:%d\", c.Size(), c.ModTime().UnixNano())\n-\t}\n+\tconfig := digestOf(\"config\")\n \treturn strings.Join([]string{filepath.Clean(root), head, shallow, config, strings.Join(args, \"\\x00\")}, \"\\x01\"), true\n }\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go b/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\nindex 6d971373..e75d67e8 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\n@@ -443,6 +443,17 @@ func (s *server) handle(ctx context.Context, conn net.Conn) {\n \t\twriteReply(conn, reply)\n \tdefault:\n \t\tif s.opts.Handler != nil {\n+\t\t\t// A hosted operation is its own handshake: it carries the caller's identity, and a\n+\t\t\t// caller of another engine, build, protocol, schema or worktree is refused before the\n+\t\t\t// handler sees it, whatever the caller handshook with a moment before.\n+\t\t\tif req.Identity == nil {\n+\t\t\t\twriteReply(conn, Reply{Error: \"a hosted operation carries the caller's identity\"})\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif mism := s.opts.Identity.Mismatches(*req.Identity); len(mism) > 0 {\n+\t\t\t\twriteReply(conn, Reply{Mismatch: mism, Error: \"incompatible\", PID: os.Getpid()})\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t\t// The reply of a long operation must still be writable.\n \t\t\t_ = conn.SetDeadline(time.Now().Add(hostedDuration(req.DeadlineMS) + requestDeadline))\n \t\t\tif reply, ok := s.opts.Handler(ctx, req); ok {\n@@ -458,7 +469,7 @@ func (s *server) handle(ctx context.Context, conn net.Conn) {\n \n // drain waits, up to the deadline, for the requests in flight besides this one.\n func (s *server) drain(deadline time.Duration) Reply {\n-\tbefore := s.inflight.Load() - 1\n+\tbefore := s.inflight.Load() + s.busy() - 1\n \tend := time.Now().Add(deadline)\n \tfor s.inflight.Load()+s.busy() > 1 && time.Now().Before(end) {\n \t\ttime.Sleep(5 * time.Millisecond)\n@@ -603,12 +614,19 @@ func hostedDuration(deadlineMS int) time.Duration {\n // Run sends a hosted operation: the command line, the digest of the caller's environment and\n // the longest it may take (zero for the runtime's default).\n func (c Client) Run(ctx context.Context, args []string, env string, deadline time.Duration) (Reply, error) {\n-\treturn c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: \"run\", Args: args, Env: env, DeadlineMS: int(deadline.Milliseconds())})\n+\tid := c.Identity\n+\treply, err := c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: \"run\", Identity: &id, Args: args, Env: env, DeadlineMS: int(deadline.Milliseconds())})\n+\tif err == nil && len(reply.Mismatch) > 0 {\n+\t\t// Refused before it started: the caller falls back, as for any incompatible runtime.\n+\t\treturn reply, &IncompatibleError{Mismatch: reply.Mismatch}\n+\t}\n+\treturn reply, err\n }\n \n // Do sends an operation the runtime hosts and returns its reply.\n func (c Client) Do(ctx context.Context, op string) (Reply, error) {\n-\treturn c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: op})\n+\tid := c.Identity\n+\treturn c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: op, Identity: &id})\n }\n \n // WaitReleased returns when the endpoint of the identity can be taken: nothing answers and the\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime_test.go\nindex ab19424c..3d4dc56d 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime_test.go\n@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ import (\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n \t\"runtime\"\n \t\"strings\"\n+\t\"sync/atomic\"\n \t\"testing\"\n \t\"time\"\n )\n@@ -415,3 +416,74 @@ func TestAReplyDoesNotEscapeHTMLCharacters(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"the reply escapes HTML characters: %s\", raw)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// A hosted operation is its own handshake: a caller whose engine differs from the runtime's is\n+// refused before the handler runs, even if it handshook with an earlier runtime a moment before.\n+func TestAHostedOperationFromAnotherEngineIsRefusedBeforeTheHandlerRuns(t *testing.T) {\n+\tskipUnsupported(t)\n+\tid := identity(t, repo(t), \"7.4.1\")\n+\tdir := shortDir(t)\n+\tvar ran atomic.Int64\n+\tctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())\n+\tdefer cancel()\n+\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n+\tgo func() {\n+\t\tdone <- Serve(ctx, Options{Identity: id, Dir: dir, Handler: func(_ context.Context, req Request) (Reply, bool) {\n+\t\t\tif req.Op != \"run\" {\n+\t\t\t\treturn Reply{}, false\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tran.Add(1)\n+\t\t\treturn Reply{Outcome: OutcomeCompleted}, true\n+\t\t}})\n+\t}()\n+\tc := Client{Identity: id, Dir: dir}\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 200; i++ {\n+\t\tif _, err := c.Status(context.Background()); err == nil {\n+\t\t\tbreak\n+\t\t}\n+\t\ttime.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := c.Run(context.Background(), []string{\"review-check\"}, \"env\", 0); err != nil || ran.Load() != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a caller of the same identity: %v, ran %d\", err, ran.Load())\n+\t}\n+\tother := c\n+\tother.Identity.Engine = \"7.5.0\"\n+\t_, err := other.Run(context.Background(), []string{\"review-check\"}, \"env\", 0)\n+\tvar inc *IncompatibleError\n+\tif !errors.As(err, &inc) || ran.Load() != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a caller of another engine: %v, ran %d\", err, ran.Load())\n+\t}\n+\t// A request with no identity at all is refused too.\n+\treply, err := c.roundTrip(context.Background(), Request{Op: \"run\"})\n+\tif err != nil || reply.OK || ran.Load() != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a hosted request without an identity: %+v %v ran %d\", reply, err, ran.Load())\n+\t}\n+\tcancel()\n+\t<-done\n+}\n+\n+// A command past its deadline is counted by the stop as what it abandoned, never as a negative\n+// drain.\n+func TestAStopCountsWhatARunningCommandAbandonsAndNeverReportsANegativeDrain(t *testing.T) {\n+\tskipUnsupported(t)\n+\tid := identity(t, repo(t), \"7.4.1\")\n+\tdir := shortDir(t)\n+\tvar busy atomic.Int64\n+\tbusy.Store(1)\n+\tctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())\n+\tdefer cancel()\n+\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n+\tgo func() { done <- Serve(ctx, Options{Identity: id, Dir: dir, Busy: busy.Load}) }()\n+\tc := Client{Identity: id, Dir: dir}\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 200; i++ {\n+\t\tif _, err := c.Status(context.Background()); err == nil {\n+\t\t\tbreak\n+\t\t}\n+\t\ttime.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)\n+\t}\n+\treply, err := c.Stop(context.Background(), 100*time.Millisecond)\n+\tif err != nil || reply.Abandoned != 1 || reply.Drained != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"stop with a command still running: %+v %v\", reply, err)\n+\t}\n+\t<-done\n+}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S4HrYuU29AARn7B7RWQ95b","permissi