{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Nkzn4VXfqu1mtDgWPngrH","type":"tool_result","content":"review.scope=milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime\nreview.required=true\nreview.profile=milestone-integration@1\nreview.digest=sha256:6043e298e745c5168c4d240a387fed683aa0df2584fe87720495dfbf0eb3a569\nreview.fresh=false\nreview.approved=false\nreview.read_view=id:sha256:9b5855687ffce8821972a4734b01cfc917f443cc88f09a52723d549d541d14f3 freshness:unknown roots:1 inputs:24204 bytes:136690041\nreview.assurance=agent:anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 — machine-attested executor declaration; assurance declared; separation required same-actor-separate-execution, declared declared-agent, verified signed-executor-execution; cognitive independence not-observable; run rrn-bdcf82bd12194216 proof rrp-bdf35f5a5cac67b01fb2f0474bd0082215aa3d8a7b1dcf028ac2aee4afc0742b; reviewer anthropic/claude-opus-5-5; implementation anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5; source native-issuer-signed-executor-declaration; implementation identity declared; independence achieved different-model; historical claim valid-claim at issuer-asserted-signed-attested-at; current operation valid-claim; historical authorization not-established; attribution legacy-undifferentiated (preparation, conclusion, confirmation and application were not recorded apart)\n[ERROR] finding F1 (medium) is open: The exit gate requires RAM/CPU/latency per scenario with simultaneous jobs; the measurement records latency per scenario, a single runtime-wide RAM peak (runtime_measure_test.go:225 reads only VmHWM/VmRSS) and no CPU at all, and no two heavy jobs run concurrently (report :53,:57). The implementer's notes disclose missing CPU limits, not missing CPU measurement.\n[ERROR] finding F2 (medium) is open: The ADR amendment still says the runtime hosts no domain operation and that slice 2 reuses B33 views, and the decision (:64-65) requires CPU quota/affinity and a global concurrency bound; the delivered slices host five checks, memoize pure Git reads and declare CPU and global limits as non-goals, without amending the ADR, which is still Proposed (:5).\n[ERROR] finding F3 (medium) is open: pose runtime run handshakes on one connection and sends run on another; Client.Run (worktreeruntime/runtime.go:605-606) carries no identity, the run handler does not check one, and the reply's Identity/Epoch are not compared with the handshake, so a runtime restarted with another engine between the two runs the command unhandshaken, which is the D1 falsifier of pose-optional-worktree-runtime.\n[ERROR] finding F6 (low) is open: A crit:medium follow-up (admission/QoS, slice 3) stays open in a done member spec although pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement delivered it; the milestone does not dispose it and the policy accepts only low risks.\n[ERROR] latest review rva-e45599573a99869a of milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime decided changes-requested; remediate its findings and seal a superseding bundle\n[ERROR] governance read view is unknown; review inputs were not proven stable","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"86e248e3-e8d8-40c2-a304-bc9540a6e8ce","timestamp":"2026-11-10T10:39:14.489Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"review.scope=milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime\nreview.required=true\nreview.profile=milestone-integration@1\nreview.digest=sha256:6043e298e745c5168c4d240a387fed683aa0df2584fe87720495dfbf0eb3a569\nreview.fresh=false\nreview.approved=false\nreview.read_view=id:sha256:9b5855687ffce8821972a4734b01cfc917f443cc88f09a52723d549d541d14f3 freshness:unknown roots:1 inputs:24204 bytes:136690041\nreview.assurance=agent:anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 — machine-attested executor declaration; assurance declared; separation required same-actor-separate-execution, declared declared-agent, verified signed-executor-execution; cognitive independence not-observable; run rrn-bdcf82bd12194216 pr