{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgu75scsR2NqnxZBrhTLx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**decision: changes-requested**\n\nOf the seven round-1 findings, five are fixed and one is partly fixed. R1-F1, the main blocker on the exit gate, is still open. The fix commit changed the measurement harness (`runtime_measure_test.go`) but no new measurement was ever committed.\n\n## Prior findings\n- **R1-F1: not fixed.** The harness now records CPU time and memory per scenario and adds T7, two heavy checks at once (`runtime_measure_test.go:38,224-270`). But the report was not touched in e91c7fff; its last change is 89a65914. `.pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md` and its `.json` still hold **two** runs, with no CPU figure, no per-scenario memory, no T7 and no `two_heavy` scenario. A search of `.pose` (excluding review bundles and runs) finds no `T7`, `cpu_ms` or `two_heavy` anywhere. The implementer's note that \"three runs are in the report, the third qualifies\" is not true of this checkout.\n- **R1-F2: fixed.** The ADR has a 2026-11-10 amendment (`.pose/adr/…:271-309`) recording the hosted checks, the memo instead of the B33 views, and the CPU, memory and I/O limits that were not delivered. Its claim about the measurement is false, though (see N1).\n- **R1-F3: fixed.** `Client.Run` now sends the caller's identity (`worktreeruntime/runtime.go:616-623`). The server refuses a request with no identity or a mismatched one before the handler runs (`runtime.go:449-456`), and `cmdRuntimeRun` falls back on an `IncompatibleError`. A test covers this: `TestAHostedOperationFromAnotherEngineIsRefusedBeforeTheHandlerRuns`.\n- **R1-F4: partly fixed.** The drain can no longer go negative, but it now counts a running command twice (see N2).\n- **R1-F5: fixed.** The memo key hashes the content of `.git/shallow` and `.git/config` (`resident_git_memo.go:67-79`).\n- **R1-F6: fixed.** The follow-up is marked `[covered: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement]` (resident-cache spec :137).\n- **R1-F7: fixed.** The final task is checked in both specs (resident-cache :83, qos :81).\n\n## New findings\n- **N1 (medium, blocker)**: `.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:303`\n  - The ADR says the measurement records the runtime's CPU time and memory per scenario, including two simultaneous heavy checks. The committed report (:19-40) and JSON contain none of that.\n  - So the exit gate's \"RAM/CPU/latency per scenario\" with simultaneous jobs still has no evidence.\n  - T7 is also not in the QoS spec: R8 (spec :43) lists only T1-T6. It was added after the review, so \"fixed before the numbers\" can't be checked against the spec.\n- **N2 (low, follow-up)**: `pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go:472` (also :477 and :503)\n  - The handler adds a command to `busy` as soon as it is admitted (`runtime_host.go:124`), not only once its deadline has passed, as the `Busy` doc comment says (:259).\n  - While its connection is still open, a running command is therefore counted in both `inflight` and `busy`. A stop during a normal run reports drained=2 (or abandoned=2) for one command, and status `InFlight` is too high by one.\n  - The new test only covers `busy` with no open connection.\n- **N3 (low, follow-up)**: `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:242`\n  - `cpuIdleShortEnd` is computed and then discarded, so the `short_idle` scenario gets no CPU figure.\n  - The clock tick is hard-coded to 100 (:71).\n  - The per-scenario memory figure is the resident set read afterwards, not the scenario's peak.\n\n## Criteria\n- **exit-gate: finding N1.** Handshake, endpoint, lifecycle, fallback, watcher and receipt are covered by code and sealed integration tests. The RAM/CPU-per-scenario and simultaneous-heavy evidence is missing.\n- **integration: passed** (`integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration`). Slice 1's identity check now covers slice 2's hosted run, and slice 3's lanes sit inside the handler.\n- **membership: passed.** `pose closeout-check` reports `lifecycle_done=true`; all three specs are done with their tasks checked.\n- **regression: passed** on the sealed `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`. I could not re-run validation myself because this session's permissions denied it.\n- **residual-risk: passed.** The departures are recorded in the ADR. The open follow-ups are crit:low with owner and date; the medium one is now covered.\n\n## Tools\n- **`review-check` and `closeout-check`: deferred.** I ran both; they refuse only because of the round-1 attestation and the governance read view, which this attestation has to supersede.\n- **`validate`: passed, on the sealed evidence.** The run was denied in this session.\n- **`suggest-review`, `assess-tech-debt`, `assess-discover`: not used**, because their runs were denied.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\", \"line\": 303, \"summary\": \"The ADR amendment (and the implementer's notes) claim the measurement records the runtime's CPU time and resident set per scenario, including two simultaneous heavy checks, and a qualifying third run; the committed report (.pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md:19-40) and its JSON hold two runs with no CPU figure, no per-scenario memory, no T7 and no two-heavy scenario (report unchanged since 89a65914). The exit gate's RAM/CPU/latency per scenario with simultaneous jobs therefore still has no evidence, and T7 is absent from R8 of pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement (spec :43 lists T1-T6), so it was not fixed in the spec before the numbers.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\", \"line\": 472, \"summary\": \"busy is incremented at admission (cli/runtime_host.go:124), not only after a deadline as the Busy doc (:259) says, so a running command whose connection is still open counts in both inflight and busy: stop reports drained or abandoned 2 for one command, and status InFlight (:503) is one too high; the new test only covers busy with no open connection.\", \"action\": \"Count in Busy only commands whose handler has answered (or subtract the open hosted connections) and test a stop during a normal hosted run.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\", \"line\": 242, \"summary\": \"Measurement harness gaps: cpuIdleShortEnd is computed and discarded so short_idle has no CPU figure; the clock tick is hard-coded to 100 (:71); the per-scenario memory figure is VmRSS read after the scenario rather than its peak.\", \"action\": \"Mark CPU for short_idle, read the clock tick from the system or document the assumption, and record a per-scenario peak.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"Harness changed (pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:38,224-270) but the measurement report and JSON were not modified in e91c7fff (git diff 9688ed17..e91c7fff --stat; last change 89a65914); .pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md:19-40 still has two runs, no CPU, no two-heavy scenario; a search of .pose finds no T7/cpu_ms/two_heavy. See N1.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:5 and :271-309 amendment records the hosted checks, the memo replacing B33 views, the undelivered CPU quota/affinity and per-command limits, and the global bound as the sum of slots; its measurement sentence (:303) is inaccurate, reported as N1.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go:616-623 Client.Run sends the caller identity and maps Mismatch to IncompatibleError; :449-456 the server refuses a missing or mismatched identity before the handler; covered by TestAHostedOperationFromAnotherEngineIsRefusedBeforeTheHandlerRuns (runtime_test.go:420).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F4\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"evidence\": \"runtime.go:472-483 no longer yields a negative drain, but before/left now count a running command in both inflight and busy (busy set at cli/runtime_host.go:124), double-counting it; see N2.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F5\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go:67-79 hashes the content of .git/shallow and .git/config; no mtime is used.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F6\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:137 is [covered: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement].\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F7\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:83 and .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md:81 are checked.\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Read the full round-2 fix diff (9688ed17..e91c7fff) for pose-mcp, specs and ADR; the server handle/drain/state and Client in worktreeruntime/runtime.go; the hosted handler and cmdRuntimeRun in cli/runtime_host.go; the resident memo key; the measurement harness, report .md and .json; the roadmap exit gate (.pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md:60-70); the QoS spec requirements and follow-ups; the resident-cache spec follow-ups and tasks; ran pose review-check and pose closeout-check for the milestone. pose validate, suggest and assess were denied by the session profile, so regression relies on the sealed evidence.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"exit-gate\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"N1\", \"rationale\": \"Handshake, protected endpoint, lifecycle/fallback, watcher-as-key and no-retry are met by code and sealed integration tests; RAM/CPU per scenario with simultaneous heavy jobs is not evidenced by the committed measurement.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined runtime.go handle/Client.Run and runtime_host.go handler: the slice-1 identity check now gates the slice-2 hosted run, slice-3 lanes sit inside the handler before the command, and the fallback paths compose; the sealed optional-worktree-runtime, resident-cache and runtime-qos integration suites pass.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"membership\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/milestone-closes-when-reached-integration\", \"rationale\": \"pose closeout-check reports lifecycle_done=true for the milestone; the three member specs (optional-worktree-runtime, resident-cache, qos-and-measurement) are done with every task checked (resident-cache :83, qos :81).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"regression\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The sealed unit, build and all integration suites of pose-mcp pass at the bundle commit; I could not re-run pose validate because the session profile denied it, so this rests on the sealed evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the ADR amendment (:271-309) and the member specs' follow-ups: undelivered CPU, memory and I/O limits and the Windows named pipe are recorded as departures; the crit:medium follow-up is now covered; the remaining open follow-ups are crit:low with owner and review date. The measurement gap is tracked by N1 under exit-gate.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it; it refuses because of the round-1 changes-requested attestation and the unknown read view, which only this review's conclusion can supersede.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it; its precondition is the completion of this review (it still reports the round-1 attestation).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed strict validation evidence for pose-mcp passes; my re-run was denied by the session profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; the session profile denied running it.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; the session profile denied running it.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; the session profile denied running it.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2271,"cache_read_input_tokens":66106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2271},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"81b5c692-79c0-4c0b-b255-a73bbe11a9f5","timestamp":"2026-11-10T10:41:28.601Z","request_id":"req_011Cgu75sNz8sEmtyci1CnU9